name: telecom_fraud_network
title: "Telecom fraud network"
description: "Mobile numbers linked by calls, texts, call forwarding, shared handsets, shared identity, SIM history and shared payment. Five fraud schemes are planted among 2,400 ordinary subscribers: Wangiri call-back fraud, international revenue share fraud, a SIM box, subscription fraud and money mules. Start from the suspect number 99979100001 and Expand one step at a time: its twin SIM and the premium number its call-backs are forwarded to, then the revenue share ring, the subscription-fraud identity and finally the SIM box. The taxi dispatch line 99970000100, called by 650 numbers, is simply a busy number."
sourceId: entity-projection
layout: force
query:
  projection:
    datasetId: telecom_links_dataset
    sourceCol: a_msisdn
    targetCol: b_msisdn
    linkKindCol: link_kind
    attrCols[1]: via
view:
  legend: true
  workingSet: true
  plugins:
    minimap: true
    hulls: true
    behaviors[1]: hover-activate
